contact essential carers to tell them someone in your household has symptoms, so that they can follow the correct procedures to prevent spread of the infection.
What you can do to help yourself get better?
You can also use an alcohol-based hand sanitiser if your hands aren't visibly dirty.
Dry your hands using a separate towel from other people.
Stay away from others.
Each person should :
If you share a kitchen, avoid using it while others are present.
The delivery driver should not come into your home.
If your friends or family are not able to help, phone the National Assistance Helpline (0800 111 4000).
They'll be able to advise you what to do next.
Clean all surfaces every day with a household cleaner that's active against viruses and bacteria, this is important if you have an older or vulnerable person in your household.
