Gastric (Stomach) Cancer
Food that is swallowed is pushed through the esophagus into the stomach.
Acid is absorbed by the glands of the stomach wall which is acidic in nature.
Helicovector pylori bacteria attack the inner membrane of the stomach.
How can it be prevented?
Serum pepsinogen levels: Low levels suggest chronic gastric atrophy which is a risk factor for stomach cancer.
Stage I. Cancer is limited to the top layer of tissue that lines the inside of the stomach.
Cancer cells may have also spread to 1-2 nearby lymph nodes.
Palliative surgery is done for cancers that cannot be removed completely
Lung Cancer
More than 80% of all lung cancers belong to the non-small cell type.
Lung cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the lungs.
Lung cancer (Men)48 698 45 363
Tobacco Use: Tobacco use in any form is harmful, whether smoked or smokeless.
In India, 87% of males and 85% of females patients with lung cancer have history of active tobacco smoking and history of passive tobacco exposure( sitting in the vicinity of smokers and inhaling smoke ) has been found in 3% of patients.
A history of passive smoking has been found in about 3 percent of patients.
Asbestos is a set of six naturally occurring fibrous mineral widely used in house construction materials, automobiles parts and textiles due to its extremely durable and fire resistant property.
Indoor burning of coal: There is sufficient evidence that indoor combustion of coal, either for cooking or heating, increases the risk of lung cancer.
Diet: Evidence suggests that some dietary factors may be protective for lung cancer and some may increase the risk of lung cancer.
Vitamin A deficiency increases the chance of developing squamous cell carcinoma of lung in smokers .
There is no proven way to completely prevent lung cancer, but there are steps to lower the risk of getting lung cancer.
Your doctor can help you in strategies and stop-smoking aids that can help you quit effectively.
In most people with lung cancer, the symptoms arise only when the disease is advanced.
Feeling of extreme tiredness
For lung cancer, three tests have been studied for use as screening tests:
Screening is to be done every year till the age of 74 years or till symptoms appear.
All lung lesions detected by LDCT screening are not cancer and all cancer cann’t be detected by LDCT.
If your doctor finds something suspicious in screening or you have any of the symptoms of lung cancer, further tests will be required to diagnose the condition.
For this, the best method is to submit early morning sputum samples obtained after a deep cough for 3 days in a row.
A possible complication of the biopsy procedure is air leak from the lung into the space between lung and chest wall (pneumothorax ).
Bronchoscopy: For this test, a flexible fiber-optic tube (bronchoscope) is passed through the mouth or the nose and down into the windpipe and further.
If there is difficulty in breathing, removal of fluid can help the patient breathe better.
There is no involvement of lymph nodes.
Tumor size is more than 5 cms
Complete lung collapse
Stage (IV)
T1 – the tumor is contained within the lung and is smaller than 3 cm across
N0 – there is no cancer in any lymph nodes
Colorectal cancer is the cancer of the colon and/or rectum which begins with the development of pre-cancerous polyps from the lining of the colon and rectum.
New cases: 27,605
Personal history of colorectal polyps or colorectal cancer:
This is especially true if the polyps are large or if they are more in number.
Cooking mons at high temperatures produces some chemicals that increase the risk of cancer.
Excess of fruits and vegetables in the diet has been linked to reducing the risk of colorectal cancer.
CT colonography:
History & Physical Examination:
Hemogram to check for anemia, since some patients with colorectal cancer have chronic blood loss and become anemic.
The levels of these markers can sometimes be raised in benign conditions as well.
The test can be done on an outpatient basis in a hospital or doctor’s clinic.
These instructions should be understood well and followed perfectly.
Colonoscopy is generally performed under mild sedation.
Genetic tests may also be done on the biopsy specimens to identify specific gene changes in the cancer cells.
Computed tomography (CT) scan can help to find out if the colorectal cancer has spread to liver and other organs.
The cancer has grown through the inner lining or into the muscle layers of the intestine and spread to lymph nodes, but not to other distant parts of the body.
These are used alone or in combination depending on the stage of the cancer, performance status of the patient, grade of the tumor and other factors.
Partial colectomy- surgery to remove the section of colon that has cancer and nearby lymph nodes is the standard treatment.
Stage III colon/rectal cancer
Stage IV colon cancer
In this stage, surgery is not possible in majority of the cases considering the spread of the disease.
Other types of esophageal cancer are uncommon.
Number of cases in men is more than double than that in women (male: female ratio 2.4:1)
Scamus cell carcinoma is three times more common in black males than in white males, whereas adenocarcinoma is more common in white males.
In Barrett’s esophagus, the risk of adenocarcinoma is higher than in people not having it.
How can it be prevented?
Major environmental risk factors (cigarette) for scamus cell carcinoma in esophageal cancer can be reduced by limiting smoking and alcohol consumption.
Eating a healthy diet rich in fruits and vegetables
Difficulty in swallowing food (dysphagia)
How can it be identified?
Using the endoscope, the doctor examines the esophagus, looking for suspicious areas and takes a piece of tissue for pathologic examination.
Endoscopic ultrasound (using an ultrasound probe at the end of an endoscope) helps the doctor to see the extent of growth of tumor into nearby areas as well as to check for enlarged lymph nodes.
Imaging tests can help to look for suspicious areas, check for spread of cancer and during treatment to look if the disease is responding or not.
In this test, you will have to drink thick chalky liquid called barium that coats the walls of the esophagus.
Helps in detecting spread of tumor, especially to brain and spinal cord
Biopsy is done in cases of suspected malignancy on endoscopy or imaging studies.
Cancer has spread to 7 or more lymph nodes OR involved the coverings of lungs (pleura) or heart (pericardium) OR spread to trachea, aorta, spine OR to distant organs like liver and lungs.
Removing a part of esophagus (esophagectomy)
Removing a part of esophagus and upper portion of stomach (esophagogastrectomy)
Radiotherapy may also be used for relieving symptoms of advanced esophageal cancer.
Trastuzumab (herceptin) may be used if your esophageal cancer is positive for HER2.
Various stages indicate how big or small the cancer is and has spread to various parts of the body.
But once prostate cancer begins to grow quickly or spreads outside the prostate, it is dangerous.
However, prostate cancer is more likely to be detected in obese men in more advanced stages and there is difficulty in getting treatment.
African Black men have a greater risk of prostate cancer than men of other ethnicities and these cancers are likely to be more aggressive or advanced stage at presentation.
However, prostate cancer is more likely to be detected in obese men in more advanced stages and there is difficulty in getting treatment.
Limit the intake of dairy foods and diets rich in calcium.
Not having a feeling of emptied bladder
Discomfort in the pelvic area
Early prostate cancers usually don’t cause symptoms and may be detected first during screening.
Although the cancer is usually confirmed by biopsy, in some biopsy samples, the cancer is undetectable.
Tumor is found in one-half or less of one lobe of the prostate.
Immediate treatment may not be necessary
Immediate or delayed hormonal blockage - Immediate hormonal blockage improves the quality of life.
This treatment reduces the pressure of the reed bone, obstruction of the ureter and rupture of the pathologic bone.
Hormone therapy is used when the production of the male hormone testosterone is to be inhibited in the body.
Testis Surgery: In this, the testicles are removed by surgery.
Hormone insensitive disease
4mg IV q 3-4 weeks (for 6-9 months then at 3 monthly interval) For adequate pain control
Hot flashes, sweats, and gynecomastia
For men diagnosed with a very early stage of prostate cancer, treatment may not be necessary right away.
Cutting off the supply of hormones may cause cancer cells to die or to grow more slowly.
Side effects of hormone therapy may include erectile dysfunction, hot flashes, loss of bone mass, reduced sex drive and weight gain.
